note <Authenticated encryption with AES-256-GCM. The clean uniform interface; the per-env native implementation is selected at build time and hidden. Each platform delegates to its built-in AEAD (node / browser Web Crypto SubtleCrypto, rust aes-gcm, swift CryptoKit AES.GCM, kotlin javax.crypto). The key (32 bytes) and nonce (12 bytes) are passed as hex text, the plaintext as utf-8 text. encrypt returns the ciphertext with the 16-byte authentication tag appended, as hex text. decrypt takes that same hex and returns the plaintext, or fails if the tag does not verify. The interface is async because the Web Crypto API only exposes encryption asynchronously, and it stays uniform across every target.>

load @cluesurf/base/code/native/cryptography/cipher
  find encrypt-aes-gcm
  find decrypt-aes-gcm

task encrypt
  mark async
  take key, like text
  take nonce, like text
  take plain, like text
  like text
  send back
    call encrypt-aes-gcm
      read key
      read nonce
      read plain
      wait true

task decrypt
  mark async
  take key, like text
  take nonce, like text
  take sealed, like text
  like text
  send back
    call decrypt-aes-gcm
      read key
      read nonce
      read sealed
      wait true
